# Coach invariants — do not regress (#54, #56)

Encoded from repeated Codex P1 findings: PR #54 (coach draft/review/practice isolation),
PR #56 (streaming markdown emphasis). Every rule below was a real P1 bug once. When touching
these files, scan this list before and after your diff.

## A. CoachView / draft / practice (#54) — CRITICAL

1. **Revision + cancel go together.** Any draft / side / practice change that invalidates
   in-flight Analyze / Playbook / Next-pick MUST bump `contextRevision` (via
   `setContextRevision` + `contextRevisionRef.current`) **AND** call `cancelStream()`.
   MUST also retire completed suggestion cards stamped with an older revision
   (`clearStaleSuggestionsForRevision`) — stale cards must not stay actionable against the
   new board.
2. **No-op means no revision.** Re-tapping the already-selected "My side" MUST NOT bump the
   revision or cancel streams. Compare desired vs current state before invalidating.
3. **My side vs editing side.** NEVER infer or lock `mySide` from the first pick when the
   user set My side explicitly — preserve `mySideExplicitRef`. A practice-hero-only board
   counts as non-empty for ally-side inference: picking an enemy first on an otherwise
   empty board MUST NOT flip `mySide` to the opposing side.
4. **Practice hero materializes.** Direct ally picks and Next-pick accepts MUST route
   through `acceptHeroOntoDraft` so the seeded practice hero lands on the ally board.
   MUST NOT raw-push onto an empty ally side (empty-board seed-only logic silently drops
   the practice hero from later analysis).
5. **Accepts bind to request-time context.** Accepting a suggestion / Next-pick MUST use
   the ally side + practice hero stamped on the message/session at request time — NOT live
   controls the user may have changed after the card was generated.
6. **Review isolation.** Entering review MUST snapshot the draft (`draftSnapshotRef`);
   leaving review MUST restore it — UNLESS the user intentionally edited the draft during
   review (persist those edits into the snapshot so restore keeps them). MUST NOT discard
   accepted draft actions on review exit. Cancel draft streams when leaving to review /
   switching lessons externally where context changed.
7. **Streaming setState.** `onChunk` MUST functional-append only:
   `setMessages(prev => appendStreamChunk(prev, …))`. NEVER `messages.find(...)` and
   overwrite — that drops interleaved chunks (see `_buggyAppendPattern_DO_NOT_USE`).
8. **Post-bump stream revisions.** After `applyLessonSwitch` bumps the revision inside a
   `setState`, the next stream MUST read `contextRevisionRef.current` **after** the bump —
   MUST NOT reuse a revision captured before the `setState` (it is stale by definition).
9. **Enablement from resolved lineup.** Analyze / Next-pick enablement MUST derive from the
   **resolved lineup** (`resolveCoachingLineup` allies/enemies after practice
   materialization), not the raw empty draft. Enemy-only drafts can still enable
   Next-pick / ally recommendations.

## B. markdownLines (#56) — HIGH — do not regress

- CommonMark-ish flanking for `*` / `**` / `_`: a delimiter run MUST NOT open before
  whitespace or close after whitespace.
- Code spans protect their contents from emphasis parsing; skip code spans when scanning
  for closers; closer backtick run length MUST equal opener run length; an unmatched
  backtick opener run is consumed atomically as literal text.
- Escapes: honor `\*` etc. outside code spans; backslashes are literal inside code spans.
- Nested `***` / `****` partition by nesting context — MUST NOT always peel first/last two
  stars as bold + remainder italic.
- Cache failed closer scans (perf): re-scanning every position on every SSE chunk is
  quadratic and froze streaming UIs once already.
- `_` boundaries are Unicode/CJK-aware, not JS `\w`: snake_case identifiers MUST NOT
  render as emphasis; CJK-adjacent `_` still needs real word-boundary logic.
- Streaming half-open delimiters stay literal: a mid-stream `**foo` MUST NOT be
  reinterpreted as italic; wait for the closing run.

## C. DeepSeek output language

- Output language MUST follow UI `lang` on analyze / playbook / review / chat: `zh` →
  简体中文, `en` → English (`lib/aiLanguage.js`). This invariant is being locked by
  PR #57; do not change the default-language product decision (中文 first) here.
